### Customer requests for the VS Code "REST Client" extension (humao.rest-client):
### click "Send Request" above each request. Run them top to bottom: later requests
### use the id of the customer created by the first one.

@base = http://localhost:8080/api

### Create a customer with two addresses: one save() stores all three rows (cascade)
# @name create
POST {{base}}/customers
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Maija",
  "lastName": "Meikäläinen",
  "email": "maija@example.fi",
  "phone": "040-1111111",
  "addresses": [
    { "streetAddress": "Mannerheimintie 1", "postalCode": "00100", "city": "Helsinki", "country": "Suomi" },
    { "streetAddress": "Hämeenkatu 5", "postalCode": "33100", "city": "Tampere", "country": "Suomi" }
  ]
}

### Get the customer with addresses
GET {{base}}/customers/{{create.response.body.$.id}}

### Update: creates a new version in the system-versioned table
PUT {{base}}/customers/{{create.response.body.$.id}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Maija",
  "lastName": "Meikäläinen",
  "email": "maija@example.fi",
  "phone": "050-2222222"
}

### Add an address (saved through the cascade)
POST {{base}}/customers/{{create.response.body.$.id}}/addresses
Content-Type: application/json

{ "streetAddress": "Aleksanterinkatu 3", "postalCode": "90100", "city": "Oulu", "country": "Suomi" }

### Remove the second address (deleted by orphanRemoval)
DELETE {{base}}/customers/{{create.response.body.$.id}}/addresses/{{create.response.body.$.addresses[1].id}}

### History: one version per change
GET {{base}}/customers/{{create.response.body.$.id}}/history

### Delete the customer: its addresses are deleted too (cascade)
DELETE {{base}}/customers/{{create.response.body.$.id}}

### The history remains after deletion
GET {{base}}/customers/{{create.response.body.$.id}}/history

### A customer with orders can't be deleted: 409
DELETE {{base}}/customers/24
